## REGLES AUTOMATIQUES A CHAQUE EXECUTION

Ces regles s'appliquent AUTOMATIQUEMENT a chaque workflow cree ou modifie:

### 1. Multi-Tenancy OBLIGATOIRE
```javascript
// PREMIER NODE de CHAQUE workflow webhook
const tenantId = $input.first().headers['x-tenant-id'];
const userId = $input.first().headers['x-user-id'];

if (!tenantId) {
  return {
    status: 400,
    body: { error: 'Missing x-tenant-id header', code: 'MISSING_TENANT' }
  };
}

// Propager dans tout le workflow
return {
  ...$input.first().json,
  _context: {
    tenantId,
    userId,
    executionId: $execution.id,
    startTime: Date.now()
  }
};
```

### 2. Validation Input OBLIGATOIRE
```javascript
// TOUJOURS valider les inputs au debut du workflow
const validateInput = (data, schema) => {
  const errors = [];
  for (const [field, rules] of Object.entries(schema)) {
    const value = data[field];
    if (rules.required && (value === undefined || value === null || value === '')) {
      errors.push({ field, error: 'Required field missing' });
      continue;
    }
    if (value === undefined) continue;
    // Type validations...
  }
  return { valid: errors.length === 0, errors };
};

const validation = validateInput($json, schema);
if (!validation.valid) {
  return {
    status: 400,
    body: { error: 'Validation failed', details: validation.errors }
  };
}
```

### 3. tenant_id dans TOUTES les queries
```sql
-- JAMAIS de query sans tenant_id
-- BAD
SELECT * FROM analyses WHERE id = $1;

-- GOOD (belt and suspenders avec RLS)
SELECT * FROM analyses WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2;
```

### 4. Error Handling avec Retry
```javascript
// Structure try-catch avec retry logic
const MAX_RETRIES = 3;
const attempt = $json._retryAttempt || 0;

try {
  const result = await performOperation();
  return { success: true, data: result };
} catch (error) {
  if (error.retryable && attempt < MAX_RETRIES) {
    const delay = 1000 * Math.pow(2, attempt);
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));
    return { ...$json, _retryAttempt: attempt + 1, _lastError: error.message };
  }
  throw error;
}
```

### 5. Logging Structure JSON
```javascript
// CHAQUE node significatif doit logger
console.log(JSON.stringify({
  level: 'info',
  executionId: $execution.id,
  workflow: $workflow.name,
  node: $node.name,
  tenantId: $json._context?.tenantId,
  action: 'action_name',
  duration: Date.now() - $json._context?.startTime,
  timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
}));
```

