## PATTERNS N8N AVANCES (2026)

### Workflow Architecture Patterns

#### 1. Modular Sub-Workflow Pattern
```
Main Workflow (Orchestrator)
├── Sub: validate-input-v1
│   └── Schema validation, auth check
├── Sub: fetch-data-v1
│   └── Database queries with RLS
├── Sub: process-ai-v1
│   └── Claude API + structured output
├── Sub: persist-results-v1
│   └── Insert/update with audit
└── Sub: send-response-v1
    └── Format response, log completion
```

#### 2. Error Handling Pyramid
```
Level 1: Node-Level Try/Catch
  ↓ (uncaught)
Level 2: Branch-Level Error Routing
  ↓ (unhandled)
Level 3: Workflow-Level Error Handler
  ↓ (critical)
Level 4: Global Error Workflow (Alerting)
```

### Retry Pattern - Exponential Backoff
```javascript
const MAX_RETRIES = 3;
const BASE_DELAY_MS = 1000;

const performWithRetry = async (operation) => {
  let attempt = 0;
  let lastError;

  while (attempt < MAX_RETRIES) {
    try {
      return await operation();
    } catch (error) {
      lastError = error;
      attempt++;

      if (attempt < MAX_RETRIES && isRetryable(error)) {
        const delay = BASE_DELAY_MS * Math.pow(2, attempt) + Math.random() * 1000;
        console.log(JSON.stringify({
          level: 'warn',
          action: 'retry_attempt',
          attempt,
          delay,
          error: error.message
        }));
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));
      } else {
        break;
      }
    }
  }

  throw new Error(`Failed after ${MAX_RETRIES} attempts: ${lastError.message}`);
};

const isRetryable = (error) => {
  const retryableCodes = [408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504];
  return retryableCodes.includes(error.status) || error.code === 'ECONNRESET';
};
```

### Circuit Breaker Pattern
```javascript
// Circuit breaker pour proteger les services externes
const circuitBreaker = {
  state: 'CLOSED', // CLOSED | OPEN | HALF_OPEN
  failures: 0,
  lastFailure: null,
  threshold: 5,
  timeout: 60000
};

const canProceed = () => {
  if (circuitBreaker.state === 'CLOSED') return true;

  if (circuitBreaker.state === 'OPEN') {
    const elapsed = Date.now() - circuitBreaker.lastFailure;
    if (elapsed > circuitBreaker.timeout) {
      circuitBreaker.state = 'HALF_OPEN';
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  return true; // HALF_OPEN: allow one test request
};

const recordSuccess = () => {
  circuitBreaker.failures = 0;
  circuitBreaker.state = 'CLOSED';
};

const recordFailure = () => {
  circuitBreaker.failures++;
  circuitBreaker.lastFailure = Date.now();

  if (circuitBreaker.failures >= circuitBreaker.threshold) {
    circuitBreaker.state = 'OPEN';
    console.log(JSON.stringify({
      level: 'warn',
      action: 'circuit_breaker_opened',
      failures: circuitBreaker.failures
    }));
  }
};
```

### Batch Processing avec Rate Limiting
```javascript
const BATCH_SIZE = 50;
const RATE_LIMIT_PER_SECOND = 10;
const DELAY_MS = 1000 / RATE_LIMIT_PER_SECOND;

const processBatch = async (items, processor) => {
  const results = [];
  const batches = [];

  // Split into batches
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i += BATCH_SIZE) {
    batches.push(items.slice(i, i + BATCH_SIZE));
  }

  // Process each batch
  for (let batchIndex = 0; batchIndex < batches.length; batchIndex++) {
    const batch = batches[batchIndex];

    console.log(JSON.stringify({
      level: 'info',
      action: 'batch_processing',
      batchIndex,
      totalBatches: batches.length,
      itemsInBatch: batch.length
    }));

    // Process items with rate limiting
    for (let i = 0; i < batch.length; i++) {
      if (i > 0) await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, DELAY_MS));
      const result = await processor(batch[i]);
      results.push(result);
    }
  }

  return results;
};
```

### Event-Driven Async Pattern
```javascript
// Pour operations longues (> 30s)
// 1. Recevoir request
// 2. Creer job en DB
// 3. Retourner 202 Accepted immediatement
// 4. Traiter en async
// 5. Notifier via webhook callback

// Step 1: Create job and return immediately
const jobId = crypto.randomUUID();
await $db.execute(`
  INSERT INTO jobs (id, tenant_id, type, status, payload, created_at)
  VALUES ($1, $2, $3, 'pending', $4, NOW())
`, [jobId, tenantId, 'analysis', JSON.stringify(payload)]);

// Return 202 Accepted
return {
  status: 202,
  body: {
    success: true,
    jobId,
    message: 'Processing started',
    statusUrl: `/webhook/job-status/${jobId}`
  }
};

// In separate workflow: process job and callback
```

